%description:
Use of C++20 formatting in exception constructors

%activity:

#if __cplusplus >= 202002L // only with C++20 or later

std::string name = "Joe";
cRuntimeError e("Value is {}, name is {}"_fmt, 42, name);
EV << e.what();

#else

EV << "#SKIPPED: Non-C++20 compiler" << std::endl;

#endif

%contains: stdout
Value is 42, name is Joe